So I've seen this type of clamp a lot in enemy code and it seems to be an inline. Does anyone have an idea why in the world they would write a clamp this way?
```

    f32 limitedDelta;
    if (0.0f < delta)
        limitedDelta = limit > delta ? delta : limit;
    else
        limitedDelta = -limit > delta ? -limit : delta;

    f32 turn = MsAngleDiff(limitedDelta, headRotation);
    if (0.0f < turn)
        turn = 1.0f > turn ? turn : 1.0f;
    else
        turn = -1.0f > turn ? -1.0f : turn;
```

i found another possible thing that could be an inline:
`TPakkun::isHideEnd() const`

according to the unused size it spans 8 instructions which means its quite small, so i have a likely guess that it's body looks something like this:
```
bool TPakkun::isHideEnd() const
{
    return checkLiveFlag(LIVE_FLAG_HIDDEN);
}
```

it makes sense because this is checked throughout the codebase

Before i spend too much time on what is most likely a dud... How unrealistic is it that TMatrix34 (and others) could be using the MsMtxSetRotRPH for certain transformations like setRotX, setRotY, setRotZ and MTXConcat for concatination, i assume pretty slim, but worth asking 🙃 
I am likely force-matching, but i really liked how TMtx34f kinda slotted into some of the callbacks lmao, but it is likely copium...

